  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "How to read it",
      "items": [
        "A box is a thread. A card is plain code: React components or data jobs, with the count on the card; there are no isolates in the native builds.",
        "T3 is shown in full and stands for every machine; T1, T2 and T4\u2013T8 are grouped.",
        "Arrows show records written to and read from the page's store.",
        "Inside each data worker, its 4 jobs share a local store; every record they publish is also posted to the page's store."
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "When something blocks",
      "items": [
        "A widget's code runs on the main thread, so a block stalls the whole page.",
        "In native the data jobs stall too; in native + workers they keep running in their workers."
      ]
    }
  ]
